<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" STYLE="width: 100%; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><TR STYLE="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0"></TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Symbol; font-size: 10pt">&middot;</FONT></TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-size: 10pt">Revenue of
                                            $492 million decreased 2% compared to the third quarter of 2025, <FONT STYLE="color: #101820">primarily
                                            due to a </FONT>5% decrease <FONT STYLE="color: #101820">in average system price mainly attributable
                                            to a higher mix of China OEM export volumes, which carry less software content and therefore
                                            lower pricing, and lower Supervision volumes. Higher EyeQ volumes partially offset these
                                            effects. SuperVision deliveries exceeded our expectations, and the pass-through of higher
                                            memory costs added approximately $7 million to third-quarter revenue at zero gross margin.</FONT></FONT></TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" STYLE="width: 100%; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><TR STYLE="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0"></TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Symbol; font-size: 10pt">&middot;</FONT></TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-size: 10pt; color: #101820">Gross
                                            Margin </FONT><FONT STYLE="font-size: 10pt">increased by nearly 5 percentage points <FONT STYLE="color: #101820">in
                                            the </FONT>third quarter <FONT STYLE="color: #101820">of </FONT>2026 <FONT STYLE="color: #101820">as
                                            compared to the prior year period. This was due to a decrease in amortization of intangible
                                            assets as a percentage of revenue, partially offset by a modest reduction in EyeQ ASP mainly
                                            attributable to higher China OEM volumes which carry lower ASP as well as higher EyeQ-related
                                            cost per unit given the different mix of EyeQ products sold.</FONT></FONT></TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" STYLE="width: 100%; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><TR STYLE="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0"></TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Symbol; font-size: 10pt">&middot;</FONT></TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-size: 10pt; color: #101820">Adjusted
                                            Gross Margin </FONT><FONT STYLE="font-size: 10pt">decreased <FONT STYLE="color: #101820">in
                                            the </FONT>third quarter <FONT STYLE="color: #101820">of </FONT>2026 <FONT STYLE="color: #101820">by
                                            </FONT>3 percentage points <FONT STYLE="color: #101820">as compared to the prior year period.
                                            This was primarily due to lower EyeQ ASP, mainly attributable to a higher mix of Chinese
                                            OEM shipments which carry lower ASP as well higher EyeQ-related cost per unit given the different
                                            mix of EyeQ products sold. Higher-than-expected SuperVision volume and the pass-through of
                                            higher memory costs together reduced corporate average gross margin by approximately 100
                                            basis points relative to expectations.</FONT></FONT></TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<TABLE CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" STYLE="width: 100%; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><TR STYLE="font-size: 10pt; vertical-align: top">
<TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0"></TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; width: 0.5in"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Symbol; font-size: 10pt">&middot;</FONT></TD><TD STYLE="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-size: 10pt; color: #101820">Operating
                                            Margin as well as Adjusted Operating Margin </FONT><FONT STYLE="font-size: 10pt">increased
                                            in the third quarter of 2026 <FONT STYLE="color: #101820">as compared to the prior year period</FONT>.
                                            <FONT STYLE="color: #101820">The increase was primarily due to an incentive grant recognized
                                            under the Israeli Law for the Encouragement and Incentivization of Research and Development
                                            2026 (&ldquo;R&amp;D Law&rdquo;), which was enacted during the second quarter and applies
                                            from the beginning of 2026. During Q3 2026, our GAAP and non-GAAP Operating Income benefited
                                            from the R&amp;D Law incentive grant by </FONT>$52 <FONT STYLE="color: #101820">million and
                                            </FONT>$51 million<FONT STYLE="color: #101820">, respectively. On a year-to-date basis, GAAP
                                            and Non-GAAP Operating Income benefited from the R&amp;D Law incentive grant by </FONT>$162
                                            <FONT STYLE="color: #101820">million and </FONT>$144 million<FONT STYLE="color: #101820">,
                                            respectively.</FONT></FONT></TD></TR></TABLE>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><FONT STYLE="font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

